@@ -15,3 +15,24 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## smallpt browser playground
+
+The homepage and `public/index.html` run [Kevin Beason's smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/) entirely client-side. The existing news routes remain available.
+
+- `native/smallpt.original.cpp`: unmodified upstream source, covered by `native/LICENSE.txt`.
+- `native/renderer.cpp`: progressive C++ adapter exposing initialization, sphere colors, render passes, and an RGBA buffer. Each pass traces four samples per pixel with smallpt's original 2×2 subpixel sampling, radiance function, and scene geometry.
+- `public/wasm/`: checked-in Emscripten ES module and compiled WebAssembly binary; no compiler is required for the ordinary app build.
+- `public/render/worker.js`: runs the compiled renderer in a module worker and transfers progressive frames to the main thread. It requires no SharedArrayBuffer or special isolation headers.
+- `public/render/preview.png`: initial preview rendered by the C++ adapter at 256 samples per pixel.
+
+With Emscripten (`em++`) installed, rebuild the binary using `pnpm run build:wasm`. Run `pnpm run build` to build the application. The standalone HTML and its sibling `render/` and `wasm/` directories can also be hosted as static files. Open through an HTTP(S) host; browsers restrict workers and WebAssembly loaded directly from `file:` URLs.
+
+Command-line validation (no browser or server):
+
+```sh
+node --experimental-vm-modules scripts/check-wasm.mjs
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+The playground automatically renders the Cornell box. **Randomize & render** picks distinct colors for the mirror and glass spheres and starts a new render. Custom color inputs take effect on the next render. Samples and resolution trade rendering time for image quality; **Stop rendering** cancels the active worker, and **Save image** exports the current canvas as PNG.
